148
00:11:16,096 --> 00:11:20,430
For example, you only answer about
product, you refuse everything else.

149
00:11:21,896 --> 00:11:25,120
It limits what the model
thinks it is allowed to do.

150
00:11:26,825 --> 00:11:29,415
Five, constrain output to a schema.

151
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:36,274
When the model has to return valid JSON,
injected instructions have a harder

152
00:11:36,312 --> 00:11:39,049
time carrying through as a free text.

153
00:11:39,803 --> 00:11:46,033
You can also, Put, harder checks on the
schema validation and do not allow the

154
00:11:46,033 --> 00:11:48,369
properties like add additional properties

155
00:11:49,369 --> 00:11:53,256
So the flow on the right is
basically the point of this slide.

156
00:11:54,878 --> 00:11:58,891
Nothing the model says reaches an
action without a check in between.

157
00:11:59,847 --> 00:12:05,143
If the check fails, block it and
log it The model layer is one piece.

158
00:12:05,590 --> 00:12:12,071
Now let's go one layer up to agents
This is where the stakes go up.

